          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Just like normal paragraph text, you can use text formatting markup in the text of the footnote."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_footnote_macro_syntax",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Footnote macro syntax"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Since footnotes are defined using an inline macro, the footnote content must be inserted alongside the text it’s annotating. This requirement can make the text harder to read. You can solve this problem by externalizing your footnotes using document attributes."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When defining a document attribute that holds a footnote, you can name the document attributes whatever you want. A common practice is to name the attribute using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fn-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix. The name of the attribute can be as verbose ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fn-disclaimer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") or concise ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fn-1"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") as you prefer."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s the previous example with the footnotes defined in document attributes and inserted using attribute references."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":fn-hail-and-rainbow: footnote:[The double hail-and-rainbow level makes my toes tingle.]\n:fn-disclaimer: footnote:disclaimer[Opinions are my own.]\n\nThe hail-and-rainbow protocol can be initiated at five levels:\n\n. double{fn-hail-and-rainbow}\n. tertiary\n. supernumerary\n. supermassive\n. apocalyptic\n\nA bold statement!{fn-disclaimer}\n\nAnother outrageous statement.{fn-disclaimer}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Externalized footnote"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Notice you still get the benefit of seeing where the footnote is placed without all the noise. And since the footnotes are now defined in the document header, they could be further externalized to an include file."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This approach works since attribute references are expanded before footnotes are parsed. However, this technique does not work if you have text formatting markup in the text of the footnote (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "*bold*"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). That markup will not be interpreted. That’s because the attributes substitution (which replaces attribute references) is applied "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "after"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " the quotes substitution (which interprets text formatting markup). In order to use text formatting markup in the text of the footnote, you need to configure the substitutions on the value of the attribute entry using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "pass:[]"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " macro."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example demonstrates how to configure the substitutions applied to the text of an externalized footnote so that text formatting markup is honored."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":fn-disclaimer: pass:c,q[footnote:disclaimer[Opinions are _mine_, and mine *alone*.]]\n\nA bold statement!{fn-disclaimer}\n\nAnother outrageous statement.{fn-disclaimer}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Externalized footnote with text formatting"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "c,q"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " target on the pass macro instructs the processor to apply the special characters substitution followed by the quotes substitution. That means the text formatting in the footnote text will already be applied when the footnote is inserted using an attribute reference."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_externalizing_a_footnote",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Externalizing a footnote"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Footnotes are "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "not officially supported in headings"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (section titles and discrete headings) in pre-spec AsciiDoc. While the footnote gets parsed, there’s no guarantee that it will work properly and may require workarounds. This limitation may be lifted once the AsciiDoc Language is defined by the specification."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you use a footnote in a heading, you’ll likely find that the footnote index is wrong (either not incremented or out of order). That’s because headings (section titles and discrete headings) get converted out of document order for the purpose of generating IDs, populating up cross references, and eagerly resolving attribute references."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "One way to resolve this problem is to assign an explicit ID and reftext to any heading that contains a footnote. For example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "See <<heading>>.\n\n[[heading,Heading]]\n== Headingfootnote:[This is a heading with a footnote]"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Assigning an explicit ID and reftext to a heading will prevent substitutions from being applied before the heading is rendered, hence allowing the footnote macros to be processed in document order. This workaround will also prevent the footnote number from reappearing in the text of an xref. However, you also have to avoid using any attribute references in the heading, as that also causes substitutions to be applied eagerly, which may result in the footnotes being processed out of document order."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_footnotes_in_headings",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Footnotes in headings"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Footnotes"
      }
    ]
  }
}
